        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T10:11:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, if this is already upstream at kernel.org, then just do UPSTREAM backports please.",
      "parentUuid": "4d1081a5_4b16a021",
      "revId": "af3789e3db1ae277d6083d8d2d88d25a1259a2db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4df3b973_8c12c9a4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3538735
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T12:12:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this patch is for legacy platform only, it may take us lots of efforts if we try to upstream related codes to kernel.org. Is there any possibility that we can be granted to use the same solutions as S, because the legacy platform is still vendor freezes at S (vendor img is S; system img is V)? \nThis will greatly reduce lots of our porting efforts during V-migration. Besides, we\u0027d plan to remove this vendor hook-related feature in the pending W+W migration. Consider that there will be a brand new branch, we don\u0027t need to maintain the original k5.10 project (with vendor hook) and k6.6 simultaneously (S+V). Thank you for your consideration.",
      "parentUuid": "8e548ca9_55b8bba2",
      "revId": "af3789e3db1ae277d6083d8d2d88d25a1259a2db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a91dea5a_aa74453a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T12:15:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As you need to support these systems going forward for a long time, getting the code upstream is the simplest way to do so, AND we can take the needed abi changes if necessary.  This change, as-is, can not be taken at all.\n\nAlso you had many years from the previous submission to get the changes merged upstream, were they rejected or did that work stall somewhere?",
      "parentUuid": "4df3b973_8c12c9a4",
      "revId": "af3789e3db1ae277d6083d8d2d88d25a1259a2db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ca056f1_cf0f56d3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3538735
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T12:26:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Our new platform (since k515) didn\u0027t use vendor hook function anymore, we can directly adopt the original V4L2 framework. Thus, there will be no need to upstream any patch to kernel.org. Currently, only the legacy platform is still using the vendor hook functions, that\u0027s why we try not to upstream a specific patch to kerenl.org just for a legacy platform, consider that no new platforms are using this feature.",
      "parentUuid": "a91dea5a_aa74453a",
      "revId": "af3789e3db1ae277d6083d8d2d88d25a1259a2db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
